      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A patient with bladder frequency and urgency associated with pelvic pain had no control of symptoms by previous bladder distention, hysterectomy, or sacral nerve root stimulator. A clinical and neurophysiological diagnosis of pudendal neuropathy was made. Treatment with a nerve protection program and pudendal nerve perineural injections of local anesthetics and corticosteroids has provided total symptomatic relief that is durable."},
